      en: "Cheongsando Island, part of the Dadohae Marine National Park, is known for its slow living slogan „Cheongsando Sallim” and was designated a UNESCO Global Geopark in 2012. The island encompasses 33 km² with a population of about 2,000. It features unique dry-stone walls called „doldam” that meander through the fields. The island's highest point is Mireukbong at 385 meters. Cheongsando is also famous for its salt fields and the production of traditional salt. The island has a mild climate with average annual temperature of 14°C.",
